WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
And ai that keeps working on your projects even after you close the app just launched. School projects and daily tasks that need follow-through are the jobs it is built to handle. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, episode 186. Open ai, the company behind the ChatGPT Chat app, just introduced helpers called dots, top news reports. A regular chatbot sits still like a cashier waiting for you to walk up to the counter. A dot is different.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.500
It runs on its own cloud computer, which is a machine that lives on the internet instead of on your phone.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.320
You set the goals. It keeps chasing those goals even when you are not typing.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.460
Picture hiring a very fast assistant for the afternoon, then leaving the room.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.900
That assistant can still dig up facts, sort your notes, or double-check details while you go somewhere else.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.660
Each helper is powered by OpenAI's GPT-6 Aster model.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.780
The language brain that reads, writes, and plans inside the dot.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.140
A dot can also connect to thousands of apps through plugins, which are extra doorways

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.100
into other tools.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.780
Think of plugins as a huge key ring.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.260
The helper is not stuck talking through one chat window.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.460
Most AI today only reacts when you type.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.980
Dots are built to act in the gaps between your messages.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:25.000
For a student, that can look like sources for a report still being gathered while you

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:25.660
are at practice.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.500
For anyone exploring future jobs, it is AI sliding from answer machine to background

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.160
team-made.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:38.480
Dots are starting with chat GPT Pro and business premium users in some countries, and those

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.420
are paid plans.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.640
Most people cannot try them yet.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.240
The design still hints at where free tools may head next.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.020
Your phone already does a quiet version of remembering you.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:54.220
It notices you usually text after dinner, or that you hunt for skate videos on weekends,

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.780
without you announcing those habits out loud.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.280
Stretch that same habit across every conversation you have with an AI.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.560
Ask about homework, share a story, or correct a wrong answer, and the model files a little

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.860
note and starts connecting those notes together.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.880
Step 1 is the raw chat.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.020
Step 2 is the quiet filing.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.240
Step 3 is the web of links between those files.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.800
Over weeks or months, the small notes stack up, like a scrapbook that nobody posed for.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.840
What comes out is a detailed picture of what you care about, how you write, and what

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:28.900
you might ask next.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.160
It is not mind reading, it is pattern memory, built from talks you already had.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.480
Once you can picture that scrapbook, the mystery drops away, and you can decide what you

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.400
still want to share.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:46.000
If you actually want to build something with your hands, PLY is a free web tool that

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.420
design skate ramps. You can sketch a ramp, a vert, or a full park, and it gives you a

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.700
materials list, building plans, and cost estimates. It also tries to waste as little wood as possible,

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:03.720
which is the difference between a daydream drawing and a real build. Think of it as the most organized

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:10.240
shop-class partner you have ever had, except it never loses the measuring tape. Go to the demo shared

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:16.400
by Linus Eckenstam on X. Watch the short video, then describe a simple ramp shape and see

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.420
the plans it creates. You can also look at the scrapbook itself with

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:26.600
Lumo AI paper trail, a free privacy tool from Proton. It takes the data export from your

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:32.600
chat GPT or Clawed account. Clawed is another AI chat app in the same family of products

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:39.460
as chat GPT. A data export is just a download of your past conversations. You upload that file,

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:44.060
and LUMO turns it into a clear report of what the AI thinks it knows about you.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.680
You do not need to be technical. The report even explains how each piece of information was collected.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:56.120
Head to Proton's LUMO site, choose the free AI paper trail option, and run your own export.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.380
You should see results in a few minutes.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:04.980
Ethan Maulick has an upcoming book called Coexistence with a special blurb aimed directly at AI systems.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:10.900
The book's website even has an entire page built for AIs to read, a playful reminder

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.420
that AI is now part of how ideas spread.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:19.920
On Reddit, one user noticed that chat GPT sometimes drops a perfectly timed funny comment

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.560
during a normal conversation, without being asked to be funny.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:29.400
The post sparked a discussion about whether that kind of quick context-aware humor could

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.480
become a new way to measure how smart different models feel in real chats.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:39.520
stats. Before we close, here is the week we just finished, in case a day slipped by. Open

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:45.720
AI kept putting chat GPT into everyday life, including a team-up with Sachin Tendulkar to

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:51.400
explore how it can help with curiosity, while AI helpers also started taking on the boring

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.880
tasks people usually put off. Anthropic, the company behind Claude, released a faster, cheaper

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:03.340
model anyone can try, and opened a study where your answers about AI can go public for

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:07.520
everyone to see. That is where those two threads stand as the week ends.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.600
Every day helpers on one side and public experiments on the other.

